<Base
  title="System architecture — ariada.org"
  description="System architecture of the ariada EAA-2025 compliance pipeline: 16 MUST-OSS modules, 6 HYBRID commodity-outer surfaces, and the closed patented cores. 74% open-source surface across the 35-component inventory."
>
  <section>
    <h1>System architecture</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      ariada is a seven-stop EAA-2025 compliance pipeline plus a
      TypeScript scanner runtime stack, distributed as separately
      versioned <code>@ariada-org/*</code> npm packages and a reusable
      GitHub Actions workflow. This page enumerates every component, its
      classification bucket, and its license &mdash; the same inventory
      cited in our <abbr title="Stichting NLnet — Dutch foundation funding public-interest internet infrastructure">NLnet</abbr>
      Commons Fund proposal and the <abbr title="Cyber Resilience Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/2847">CRA</abbr>
      Article 24 Open Source Steward declaration.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>74% of the combined 35-component inventory ships under an
      open-source license</strong> (16 MUST-OSS + 6 HYBRID commodity-outer
      surfaces = 22 OSS-touching components out of 30 non-RETIRE rows;
      the remaining 8 are server-side operational surface or
      patent-blocked closed cores). The full architectural specification
      lives in <a href="https://github.com/ariada-org/ariada/blob/main/docs/PLATFORM_SPEC.md" rel="external">docs/PLATFORM_SPEC.md</a>
      in the public repository.
    </p>
  </section>

