  <section aria-labelledby="pipeline-heading">
    <h2 id="pipeline-heading">Pipeline flow</h2>
    <p>
      The canonical user flow runs five stages. Every stage is
      independently usable &mdash; a downstream team may stop after any
      stage. The contracts between stages are file-on-disk artefacts,
      not in-process imports, so the pipeline degrades gracefully when
      one stage is held back a release.
    </p>
    <ol class="pipeline">
      <li>
        <strong>M1 &mdash; Scan</strong>
        <span class="muted">(owner: you, OSS scanner)</span><br />
        <code>core-engine</code> orchestrates
        <code>wcag-rules-extended</code> against your built site, via
        the <code>core-browser</code> extension or the
        <code>core-playwright</code> Node adapter.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>M2 &mdash; CI gate</strong>
        <span class="muted">(owner: you, OSS reusable workflow)</span><br />
        <code>eaa-pipeline</code> wraps M1 + downstream stages as a
        single <code>uses:</code> line. Fails the pull request on new
        violations. Differential-gate threshold semantics are the
        Module B closed inner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>M5 &mdash; Evidence</strong>
        <span class="muted">(owner: you, OSS bundler)</span><br />
        <code>evidence-emitter</code> writes the VPAT 2.5 INT report,
        the EN 301 549 JSON conformance record, and a CycloneDX SBOM
        of the scanner itself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>M3 &mdash; Statement</strong>
        <span class="muted">(owner: you, OSS generator)</span><br />
        <code>statement-generator</code> produces the EN 301 549 art. 7
        accessibility statement, deterministic and byte-identical
        across runs.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>M4 &mdash; Penalty estimate</strong>
        <span class="muted">(owner: you, OSS data package)</span><br />
        <code>penalty-estimator</code> computes per-jurisdiction
        administrative-fine exposure ranges. 11 EU member states at
        v0.1; 27 EU + 3 <abbr title="European Economic Area">EEA</abbr>
        at Wave 4.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p
      data-patent-disclosure="secondary"
      data-patent-fallback="Optional hosted stages (certificate authority, evidence-ledger anchor, AI-authorship attribution) are closed by deployment. Self-hosting adopters run the OSS pipeline without these. Per-module mapping is available on request from EU/EEA residents via <a href='mailto:legal@ariada.org'>legal@ariada.org</a>."
    >
